First order of business is for you to get your Int/Wisdom up. The next piece 
of armor on your list is a Helm of Brilliance with max enchantment. Until 
then you'll want to quaff blessed Gain Abilities until those two max out.
Also a Robe will help with your spellcasting.

What metal armor are you wearing? Unless it's Gauntlets or the HoB, you need
to ditch it to improve your spellcasting chances. Ideally you'd like to get
that Finger of Death down below single digits. You'll need it for the
Ascencion run.

Also as odd as it sounds you'll need to let at least one spell that you are
not real interested in lapse. Maybe healing in the list above since you
have Xhealing and cure sickness. You'll need to be able to confuse yourself
at will later in the game and forgotten spells are handy for that.

-
-I have spellbooks of polymorph and teleport away, but can't read them yet.

Neither are critical. First off you'll have a bunch of wands for both of
these as the game progresses. Secondly once you're set with turning potions
into water (cancellation, unicorn horn, or simply dipping into water) you
can catch teleportitis as long as you have a =oTC. Also wizards get the TC
intrinsic at 17th level.

-I'd like to add at least remove curse, cone of cold and fireball if
