-Any tips for survival as a wizard?  I'm used to fighters, and I don't want
-to lose this guy (it would be nice to go three-for-four...).

You're on the right track. Int/Wis/Dex are the critical attributes for a
spellcaster. Gear up with armor that improves those (robe, GauntDex, HoB).

Make sure that all armor is fixed.

Magic markers are your friend. With blessed ones and the whole heaping
set of spellbooks you have stashed somewhere, you can write any new spellbooks
that you need. Again Int/Wis/Dex improves your chances of writing a spellbook
that you don't yet know.

Get all the intrinsics, except maybe for teleportitis. Keep sacrificing and
praying until you get crowned.

I'd get the AC geared down some more. Have you bought all the protection you
can get? If not, then do so, though it'll cost you 5000Z a pop now. Thought
about tackling Fort Ludious? You'll definitely want a =oConflict before you
do though. Fully geared up with HS, SDSM, CoMR/Robe, speed boots, GauntDex,
and HoB you should be able to get your AC in the -40 range. I just ran an
extended test in wizard mode, and with the above array enchated to +5 each
along with a natural AC of 1, I was able to get down to -43.

Also I now know to wish for a pet Archon. Wow are they tough!

Good Luck.

